WEBVTT

00:00:00.015 --> 00:00:03.395
Easy Science. Where Does Rain Come From?

00:00:03.395 --> 00:00:08.719
The water that falls as rain today has fallen many, many times before.

00:00:08.719 --> 00:00:12.034
Water moves around and around in a great circle.

00:00:12.034 --> 00:00:13.869
It begins with the sun.

00:00:13.869 --> 00:00:17.655
The sun warms the water in seas, lakes and rivers.

00:00:17.655 --> 00:00:21.676
Some of the water turns into a gas that we cannot see.

00:00:21.676 --> 00:00:23.901
This gas goes up into the air.

00:00:23.901 --> 00:00:26.749
High in the sky, the air is cold.

00:00:26.749 --> 00:00:30.465
There the gas turns back into very small drops of water.

00:00:30.465 --> 00:00:33.902
Millions of these tiny drops together make a cloud.

00:00:33.902 --> 00:00:38.122
Inside the cloud, the small drops join and become bigger.

00:00:38.122 --> 00:00:43.223
In the end they are too heavy to stay up, and they fall to the ground as rain.

00:00:43.223 --> 00:00:46.583
If the air is very cold, they fall as snow.

00:00:46.583 --> 00:00:50.990
The rain runs into rivers, and the rivers run down to the sea.

00:00:50.990 --> 00:00:55.530
Some of it goes deep into the ground and comes out again far away.

00:00:55.530 --> 00:01:00.489
Then the sun warms the water once more, and everything begins again.

00:01:00.489 --> 00:01:02.764
The earth does not get new water.

00:01:02.764 --> 00:01:09.040
The water you drink today may once have been rain that fell on animals that lived millions of years ago.
